]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-25T13:37:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136153448,imgsize-334073.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pak astronaut Ali reaches China’s Tiangong station]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136152904.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Muhammad Zeeshan Ali, the first Pakistani astronaut, has reached the Tiangong space station in China. He launched aboard the Shenzhou-24 spacecraft alongside two Chinese astronauts, Tang Hongbo and Wu Yi. The mission is significant as it marks Pakistan's entry into human spaceflight and international collaboration in space exploration. Ali will engage in several science experiments and is expected to stay for a short duration.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/pak-astronaut-ali-reaches-chinas-tiangong-station/articleshow/136152904.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/pak-astronaut-ali-reaches-chinas-tiangong-station/articleshow/136152904.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-25T13:19:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chethan Kumar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136152949,imgsize-123322.cms"/></item></channel></rss>